    "result_text": "Done. The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe app derives read-only computed fields on `Owner` and exposes them through the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` (MapStruct auto-maps matching property names), exactly as the existing `displayName` field does. I followed that same pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a computed `getInitials()`:\n   ```java\n   public String getInitials() {\n       return Character.toUpperCase(this.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n           + Character.toUpperCase(this.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\";\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gets `getInitials/setInitials`, letting MapStruct wire it through to the JSON response automatically.\n\n`GET /api/owners/{id}` for `john`/`smith` now returns `\"initials\": \"J.S.\"`, and the `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` test is green along with the rest of the suite.",
